/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 199 0 R
/T (A turning point in the exploitation of the mining sector to finance the war was the Rapid Support Forces takeover of the National Gold Refinery in Khartoum on 24 May 2023. The forces seized approximately 1.3 tonnes of unrefined gold and 15 tonnes of silver ready for export, with an estimated value at the time of approximately $150 million. The Sudanese Minister of Finance confirmed this and indicated that the quantity amounted to approximately 2.7 tonnes. The Minister of Minerals stated that these quantities had been previously documented and allocated to the Central Bank, the Ministry of Finance, private companies and the state's strategic portfolio, but that the Rapid Support Forces seized them in their entirety less than 40 days after the outbreak of the war.)
/E (A turning point in the exploitation of the mining sector to finance the war was the Rapid Support Forces takeover of the National Gold Refinery in Khartoum on 24 May 2023. The forces seized approximately 1.3 tonnes of unrefined gold and 15 tonnes of silver ready for export, with an estimated value at the time of approximately $150 million. The Sudanese Minister of Finance confirmed this and indicated that the quantity amounted to approximately 2.7 tonnes. The Minister of Minerals stated that these quantities had been previously documented and allocated to the Central Bank, the Ministry of Finance, private companies and the state's strategic portfolio, but that the Rapid Support Forces seized them in their entirety less than 40 days after the outbreak of the war.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
