1672 0 obj
<<
/Title (Despite the devastating war, Sudanese gold from areas controlled by different parties ends up in Dubai via various routes. Even in the face of diplomatic tensions between Sudan and the United Arab Emirates, official data shows that in 2024, more than 96% of Sudan's gold was exported to the UAE, while 84% of fuel was imported from the UAE. Numerous reports also indicate that the main funding for the Rapid Support Forces comes through the UAE, including weapons and military equipment from European countries, such as France and Germany. Thus, the consolidation of the regional trade centre and its continuous supply clearly indicates the use of gold to finance the conflict and the use of instability to drain the country's rich resources. The experience of Volkswagen is one example of how the UAE has been used as a key hub in production chains.)
/Dest [30 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 594 0 R
/Prev 1895 0 R
/Next 1126 0 R
>>
endobj
