/Title (gold and stabilising exports,reflecting the transformation of gold into a cross-border financing channel on a larger scale. Recent investigations by reliable platforms, further verified by CESS through interviews with gold traders, concluded that large quantities of Sudanese gold and other materials have been crossing into Chad and South Sudan since the outbreak of the war, before being re-exported via Dubai, in a smuggling pattern that explains the gap between local production figures and the volume of exports recorded in neighbouring countries.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2197 0 R
/Prev 2199 0 R
